# >>> gyrum-managed:start (telemetry — see warp#1014)
# Per-worktree telemetry — never committed. Regenerated by gyrum-start-work
# on every fresh clone. See warp#1014 (legacy single-file path) and
# warp#1207 (per-branch directory) for the stale-on-disk failure mode.
.gyrum/branch-meta.json
.gyrum/branch-meta/
# warp#5701 (correlated with warp#5326): the Tier-0 cite-index read by the
# warp#4316 cite-gate. Per-worktree telemetry exactly like branch-meta.json
# — re-seeded by gyrum-start-work from the run's --ticket on every fresh
# clone. It was NOT gitignored before, so it got committed onto main and a
# fresh clone inherited a stale/foreign value (warp#5137 on a warp#4279
# branch), which the cite-gate read instead of the run's ticket and blocked
# the merge. Gitignoring it stops the seeding-from-main at the source.
.gyrum/branch-meta.warp
# warp#1311: --no-ticket audited-bypass marker for the pre-push branch-meta
# gate. Existence (not contents) is the signal; it must stay local-only or
# it would leak into PR diffs and defeat the audit shape.
.gyrum/branch-meta.no-ticket
# warp#4281: the bare 3-word session run-id (e.g. brave-amber-otter),
# seeded by gyrum-start-work and (re)derived by every warp-* wrapper. A
# per-worktree runtime identity, never committed — it is regenerated per
# clone and committing it would let one worktree's id leak into another.
# warp#9963: broadened from the exact `.gyrum/session-id` to the glob so it
# also covers stale `.gyrum/session-id.<run>.bak` backup siblings, which the
# exact entry missed and which then surfaced as parent-clean-guard dirt.
.gyrum/session-id*
# warp#8208: agent-prepared PR body — per-worktree scratch the auto-create-PR
# path reads; never commit (a tracked copy is honoured on the next unrelated
# branch's PR). PR #1249 (warp#8108) added it to devtools' OWN .gitignore but
# not to this sync source, so other fleet repos never picked it up.
.gyrum/pr-body.md
# warp#13322: persisted-body finalization decision passed from review-pr to
# complete-pr and its detached watcher. Per-worktree runtime state only.
.gyrum/pr-body-finalization-required
# warp#1270: heartbeat daemon writes .pid, .log, and (warp#1251) .body
# into .gyrum/ on every tick. Each one shows up as M/D in `git status`,
# which made gyrum-complete-pr's auto-cleanup bail with "uncommitted
# changes detected" on every merge. Glob covers all three plus any
# future heartbeat.* sibling without a follow-up gitignore-sync bump.
.gyrum/heartbeat.*
.gyrum/setup-fingerprint
.gyrum/devtools-version
# warp#14722: the one-shot first-commit publisher's state file (branch name
# awaiting its first push) plus the post-commit hook spliced at scaffold
# time. Both are per-worktree runtime state — committing either would make
# every fresh clone inherit a stale push arm (or a hook pointing at a gone
# worktree), and both showed up as untracked dirt in git status otherwise.
.gyrum/deferred-first-push
.gyrum/deferred-first-push.devtools
.githooks/post-commit
# warp#1498 (EFF-3): .fleet/ holds per-host fleet-folder state (ADR-131)
# regenerated by gyrum-setup --sync-fleet-folder. .last-sync-check is the
# scratch marker deployed-sync writes to record its last successful run.
# Both surfaced as M/D in `git status` during stacked-PR sync waves and
# tripped ~15 stash/conflict-resolve operations per night before this
# entry was added. Treat as fleet telemetry, not source.
.fleet/
.last-sync-check
# gyrum runtime artefacts — managed by gyrum-setup --sync-gitignore
# Source: gyrum-labs/devtools (warp#2939)
#
# Per-clone install output and per-agent ephemeral state. None of these
# files belong in a PR diff — they were the most common merge-conflict
# files in the warp#2761 / warp#2667 / warp#2825 recovery dispatches.
#
# Load-bearing exclusions:
#   * .gyrum/branch-meta.json — kept TRACKED (warp#1311); ticket reference.
#   * Other explicitly shipped per-repo .gyrum config.
# warp#5719: devtools installs its command shims into .gyrum/bin/, writes
# .gyrum-env, and refreshes AGENT-SOP.md during setup/start-work. These are
# generated per-clone outputs, not source.
.gyrum/bin/
.gyrum-env
AGENT-SOP.md
.gyrum/heartbeat.log
.gyrum/wip-checkpoint.log
.gyrum/wip-checkpoint.pid
# warp#7073: the wip-checkpoint daemon writes an automerge-cache marker
# (referenced commit-excluded at wip-checkpoint.sh:222) but it was absent
# from BOTH this template and .gitignore — doubly-leaky, so it got
# committed onto main and then dirtied the tree on every tick, blocking
# the complete-pr auto-rebase gate (lib/checks.sh merge_base_lag_check).
.gyrum/wip-checkpoint.automerge-cache
.gyrum/auto-merge-watcher.pid
.gyrum/auto-merge-watcher.log
.gyrum/auto-merge-watcher.update-branch-count
.gyrum/agent-workspace
# warp#7073: gyrum-setup writes these per-clone install markers. They
# were gitignored elsewhere (the hand-maintained block) but absent from
# this canonical runtime-artefact list, so the merge_base_lag_check
# auto-stash (lib/checks.sh) could not recognise their churn as noise.
# Listing them here lets the auto-stash treat them as runtime artefacts.
.gyrum/setup-fingerprint
.gyrum/devtools-version
# warp#8420: the first-use smoke gate writes a per-clone Playwright deps
# stamp and, on ubuntu 26.04 (bundled chromium unavailable), a transient
# chrome-channel override config that re-exports the repo's playwright
# config with channel:'chrome' forced. Both are regenerated per run and
# must never land in a PR diff.
.gyrum/playwright-deps.stamp
.gyrum/playwright-chrome-channel.config.mjs
# warp#9771: Claude Code's isolation-worktree feature creates git worktrees
# under .claude/worktrees/ (untracked). Without this entry gyrum-start-work's
# parent-clean check (_parent_repo_has_real_dirt via git status --porcelain)
# flags it as "real uncommitted changes" and refuses to start, forcing manual
# cleanup every time. The two features fight each other; gitignoring the path
# resolves it at the source.
.claude/worktrees/
# warp#9937 (EPIC warp#9936): generic test-runner output classes. Playwright,
# vitest and similar test runners write these per-run artefacts into the repo
# root; none is source and none belongs in a PR diff, yet the fleet template
# didn't cover them, so they leaked into every repo's dirty tree. Generic-only
# — repo-specific output dirs (research/cache/ etc.) are landed/gitignored by
# the owning repo, not here. (gitignore has no inline comments, so each
# pattern's note sits on the line above it.)
# warp#9937: Playwright per-run test output dir
test-results/
# warp#9937: Playwright HTML reporter output dir
playwright-report/
# warp#9937: Playwright blob reporter (sharded runs / merge) output dir
blob-report/
# warp#9937: Playwright last-run state file
.last-run.json
# warp#9963: background-regenerated artifacts the operator's canonical clone
# accretes between sessions. None is source; each is recreated on demand, yet
# without these entries gyrum-start-work's parent-clean check
# (_parent_repo_has_real_dirt via git status --porcelain) flags them as "real
# uncommitted changes" and refuses to start — three agents hand-edited
# .git/info/exclude to get past it. Kept SPECIFIC so tracked bin/*.sh scripts
# are never over-matched. (gitignore has no inline comments; each pattern's
# note sits on the line above it.)
# warp#9963: JetBrains IDE workspace state (untracked)
.idea/
# warp#9963: per-host ADR counter/log written by next-adr-number.sh
adr-registry/
# warp#9963: fetched gyrum-substrate-run Go binary (lib/fetch-substrate-run-binary.sh);
# NOT bin/ as a whole, which holds tracked wrapper scripts
bin/gyrum-substrate-run
# warp#11817: review-pr resolution-tracker sidecar, rewritten every review
# pass (lib/findings-emit.sh findings_tracker_snapshot). Force-committed to
# devtools main once, so clones carry it TRACKED and each pass's rewrite
# trips complete-pr's merge_base_lag_check clean-tree gate (three agents hit
# it in one day). Listing it here lets the auto-stash bucket treat it as
# runtime noise instead of operator WIP, and syncs the ignore rule fleet-wide.
gyrum-review-findings.json.prior-keys
.gyrum/pr-body-finalization-required
# The review tool rewrites gyrum-review-findings.json on every pass. It is
# per-invocation state, not source: it is written into the worktree on each
# run and read from there by the recovery and structure tools, so a committed
# copy is a stale copy. A tracked copy also trips the tracked-generated-dirt
# gate, which refuses any pull request that carries one.
gyrum-review-findings.json
# >>> gyrum-managed:end
